From e3b0582f25c995f6714f9d04ea4fa4f7c8757c42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 04:28:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 68/68] jm-v7 095: read_invocation uses the old CLPER encoding
 on G71/G72/G31

bi_lower_subgroups and the quad ops go through bi_clper(), which knows
that G71/G72/G31 (BIFROST_LIMITED_CLPER) only have CLPER_OLD.i32, but
nir_intrinsic_read_invocation emitted CLPER.i32 unconditionally. The
packer asserts against that on those GPUs; release builds packed an
encoding the hardware does not have. read_invocation is subgroupBroadcast
and, through nir_lower_subgroups (lower_shuffle, lower_reduce), every
shuffle, relative shuffle, rotate, clustered and arithmetic op, plus the
jm-v7 085 texture-index waterfall.

CLPER_OLD is fixed to inactive=zero, subgroup4 and no lane op, which is
exactly read_invocation for the 4-wide v6 subgroup. Vote and ballot are
WMASK, which the Bifrost ISA has on every v6/v7 part, so no subgroup
feature needs gating on v6.

Known gap: G31 is arch 7 with an 8-wide pan_subgroup_size but the
subgroup4-only CLPER_OLD; not a target here, left as is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.c b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.c
index d7adf88..710a7f1 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.c
@@ -1997,6 +1997,16 @@ bi_emit_intrinsic(bi_builder *b, nir_intrinsic_instr *instr)
       enum bi_lane_op lane_op = BI_LANE_OP_NONE;
       enum bi_subgroup subgroup =
          bi_subgroup_from_cluster_size(pan_subgroup_size(b->shader->arch));
+      /* jm-v7 095: G71/G72/G31 only have the old CLPER encoding (the
+       * packer asserts on CLPER.i32 there). It is fixed to inactive=zero,
+       * subgroup4, no lane op, which is exactly read_invocation for the
+       * 4-wide v6 subgroup.
+       */
+      if (b->shader->quirks & BIFROST_LIMITED_CLPER) {
+         bi_clper_old_i32_to(b, dst, bi_src_index(&instr->src[0]),
+                             bi_src_index(&instr->src[1]));
+         break;
+      }
       bi_clper_i32_to(b, dst,
                       bi_src_index(&instr->src[0]),
                       bi_byte(bi_src_index(&instr->src[1]), 0),
